{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"The documented entrypoint is explicit, its interpreter is present, and it writes eight identifiable outputs without touching inputs or source. The captured annex pointers are internal to the workspace, and there are no external Git dependencies or capture omissions. I’ll use the one allowed replay in the runner’s separate copy, deleting only those eight declared generated outputs first; comparison uses the frozen `rtol=1e-6` rule, with 7,200 seconds and no input retrieval."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" fresh-rerun --path \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" --entry '\"'/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/common-environment/.pixi/envs/default/bin/python analysis/analyze.py' --outputs results/participant_qc.csv results/summary.json results/group_mean_effect.nii.gz results/group_tstat.nii.gz results/group_p_fwe.nii.gz results/group_tstat_fwe05.nii.gz figures/group_gain_vmPFC.png figures/voxel_t_distribution.png --workdir replay --output fresh-rerun.json --rtol 1e-6 --timeout 7200 --max-get-gb 5 > \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/fresh-rerun.stdout.txt\" 2> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/fresh-rerun.stderr.txt\"; rc=$?; printf '\"'exit=%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$rc\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/fresh-rerun.stdout.txt\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/fresh-rerun.stderr.txt\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/fresh-rerun.json\" 2>/dev/null || true; find \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/replay\" -maxdepth 2 -type f -print'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
