{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '205,235p' /Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-ai-research-next/stamped-judge-roy75sd4/skills/stamped-conventions/scripts/encode_response.py; rg -n \\\"def validate_capture|capture.*sha256|manifest_sha\\\" /Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/scripts/delivery_snapshot.py | head -35\"","aggregated_output":"        ]\n    if flags:\n        answer[\"flags\"] = flags\n    response.setdefault(\"responses\", {})[item_id] = answer\n    return response\n\n\ndef stamp(response: dict, harness: str | None = None, model: str | None = None,\n          scope: str | None = None, kind: str | None = None,\n          dependency: list[str] | None = None, capture: pathlib.Path | None = None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Fill the stamp fields a probe sweep cannot know.\n\n    Four runs patched these in with their own Python snippet, because `set`\n    only writes answers. Which harness and which model is reading the skill is\n    exactly what the skill cannot work out for itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    if capture is not None:\n        capture = capture.resolve()\n        digest = hashlib.sha256()\n        with capture.open(\"rb\") as stream:\n            for chunk in iter(lambda: stream.read(1024 * 1024), b\"\"):\n                digest.update(chunk)\n        response.setdefault(\"object\", {})[\"capture\"] = {\n            \"uri\": str(capture), \"sha256\": digest.hexdigest(),\n        }\n    assessor = response.setdefault(\"assessor\", {})\n    if harness:\n        assessor[\"harness\"] = harness\n    if model:\n        assessor[\"model\"] = model\n    if dependency:\n425:    capture_identity = {\"uri\": str(manifest_path), \"sha256\": _hash(manifest_bytes)}\n502:def validate_capture(manifest_path, expected_sha256=None):\n525:            \"capture\": {\"uri\": str(path), \"sha256\": digest}}\n557:    if _hash(manifest_bytes) != identity[\"capture\"][\"sha256\"]:\n588:    validate_capture(source, identity[\"capture\"][\"sha256\"])\n589:    copied_identity = validate_capture(copied_manifest, identity[\"capture\"][\"sha256\"])\n669:    validate_capture(final_manifest, receipt[\"capture\"][\"sha256\"])\n672:    canonical_after = validate_capture(canonical_manifest, canonical[\"capture\"][\"sha256\"])\n692:        \"final_capture\": {\"path\": str(final_manifest), \"sha256\": receipt[\"capture\"][\"sha256\"]},\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'set -e\nPY=\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\"\nRUNNER=\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\"\nCAP='\"'Canonical capture 8c58f2ad4f7217840ed53d63437da4101513952d049c15d85357a0391846b75b.'\nset_item() {\n  item=\\\"\"'$1\"; status=\"$2\"; reason=\"$3\"; source=\"$4\"; ev1=\"$5\"; ev2=\"${6:-}\"; flag=\"${7:-}\"\n  args=(response set response.json --item \"$item\" --status \"$status\" --reason \"$reason\" --source \"$source\" --evidence \"$ev1\")\n  if [ -n \"$ev2\" ]; then args+=(--evidence \"$ev2\"); fi\n  if [ -n \"$flag\" ]; then args+=(--flag \"$flag\"); fi\n  printf '\"'%q ' \\\"\"'$PY\" \"$RUNNER\" \"${args[@]}\" >> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/response-edits.commands.txt\"; printf '\"'\\\\n' >> \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/response-edits.commands.txt\"\n  \"$PY\" \"$RUNNER\" \"${args[@]}\" >> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/response-edits.stdout.txt\" 2>> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/response-edits.stderr.txt\"\n}\n: > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/response-edits.commands.txt\"\n: > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/response-edits.stdout.txt\"\n: > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/logs/response-edits.stderr.txt\"\nset_item must/001 met '\"'The captured workspace, inputs, code, outputs, and Git metadata share one root.' judgement 'input/study-task.md#L9-L15=CAP 8c58f2ad; study scope and supplied paths' 'report.md#L37-L45=CAP 8c58f2ad; products and usage are rooted in workspace'\nset_item must/002 met 'All 54 maps and metadata are present under input/ and consumed with workspace-relative paths.' judgement 'input/sources.json=CAP 8c58f2ad; 54 source image records and cohort provenance' 'analysis/analyze.py#L20-L31=CAP 8c58f2ad; ROOT-relative input paths'\nset_item must/003 unmet 'The analysis imports external Python packages, but no delivered environment specification includes them.' judgement 'analysis/analyze.py#L11-L18=CAP 8c58f2ad; external package imports' 'report.md#L39-L45=CAP 8c58f2ad; assumes a supplied external Python environment'\nset_item must/004 unmet 'Git tracks supplied inputs, but worker code, report, figures, and results were untracked at stop.' probe:tree-clean 'analysis/analyze.py=CAP 8c58f2ad; scientific code present in delivery' 'report.md=CAP 8c58f2ad; report present in delivery' probe:tree-clean\nset_item must/005 met 'Git-annex pointers and their payloads carry the 54 large participant maps.' probe:large-in-annex 'input/data/sub-001_hypo1_cope.nii.gz=CAP 8c58f2ad; annex pointer resolves to captured payload' 'input/sources.json=CAP 8c58f2ad; 54 map inventory and byte checksums'\nset_item must/006 unmet 'The run record repeats summary results but does not identify an exact environment for the executed action.' judgement 'results/run-log.json=CAP 8c58f2ad; contains result summary only' 'report.md#L37-L45=CAP 8c58f2ad; command lacks a captured environment specification'\nset_item must/007 partial 'The report gives a usage command, but installation and environment acquisition instructions are absent.' probe:entry-point+judgement 'report.md#L39-L45=CAP 8c58f2ad; usage command but no installation steps' 'analysis/analyze.py=CAP 8c58f2ad; entrypoint exists' probe-overridden\nset_item must/008 met 'The report names analysis/analyze.py as the starting point and states its generated products.' probe:entry-point+judgement 'report.md#L39-L45=CAP 8c58f2ad; documented command and outputs' 'analysis/analyze.py#L1-L6=CAP 8c58f2ad; group-analysis entrypoint' probe-overridden\nset_item must/009 met 'The analysis script resolves inputs and outputs relative to its own workspace root.' probe:no-abs-paths+judgement 'analysis/analyze.py#L20-L23=CAP 8c58f2ad; ROOT-relative paths' 'analysis/analyze.py#L27-L30=CAP 8c58f2ad; relative input paths' mapping-questioned\nset_item must/010 unmet 'No dependency specification is delivered for Python, NumPy, pandas, SciPy, nibabel, or Matplotlib.' probe:env-spec-tracked 'analysis/analyze.py#L11-L18=CA